  "surprise": "P50-family ablation, clean re-test of 189-fable on the 191-claude incumbent (MTP module deleted, 191 otherwise unchanged, -48 lines; handoff model identical, 9,557,760 params) scored 669/652/648 on seeds 0/1/2: mean 656.33 vs 191's 683.67 (694/694/663), -27.3, paired -25/-42/-15, below the registered keep threshold 680.33, so discard. The registered falsifier fired (mean below 660): on the no-warmup incumbent the module is not dead weight at width 384. This reverses 189's reading: its four finished no-MTP seed-runs on the 186 base (with the 200-step warmup) scored 678/695/680/700 (mean 688.3); all seven no-MTP seed-runs average 674.6 against an incumbent line of 680-687 (153/185/186/191). Either 189's runs were lucky and this one unlucky around a true effect near -8, or MTP and warmup substitute for each other (each steadies the early trajectory, and 191 had just removed the warmup); three seeds cannot separate these, though all three paired differences are negative (sign test p = 1/8). The loss came late in RL, not in round 1: round-1 targets solved 298/732/631 (sample acc 0.085/0.272/0.207), no worse than 191's 682/454/225, so the registered stacking risk (a thinner round-1 harvest) did not occur; but round-4 RL-solved was 1132/1090/1146 (mean 1123; registered 1,130-1,200) vs 191's 1189/1160/1142 (1164), with eval/round-4 ratios 0.591/0.598/0.565 (191 seed 0: 0.584). Bins >= 10: 105/106/101, >= 11: 19/25/22, >= 12: 5/4/5 (191 seed 0: 111/27/5); L* 12/11/12. Mechanical predictions mostly held: 6,749/6,697/6,064 pretraining steps (mean 6,503; registered 6,300-6,800, seed 2's pod ~10% slow; 191: 5,362/5,298/5,220, +23%), 5.4-6.0 epochs, first step at 24-30 s, final val loss 0.086/0.081/0.083 with the minimum at 195/300/165 s, held-out greedy after pretraining 0.9605/0.962/0.956 (191: 0.9705/0.972/0.9585) and 0.988-0.9915 after RL, RL sampling 195-311 samples/s, totals 1,650/1,877/1,652 s of 2,400. Missed: the final curve-point train loss was 0.059/0.06